\section{Columns of \code{records}}{
The first two columns say which input each row came from - \code{source_index} is 1-based in R, so it indexes \code{files} directly - and rows are grouped by input, in input order, whatever \code{threads} is.
\describe{
\item{\code{source_index}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based input position.}
\item{\code{source_path}}{string; never \code{NA}. Absolute path.}
\item{\code{source_name}}{string; never \code{NA}. The sample as its first row spelled it, trimmed. Matched case-insensitively (mzLib's key).}
\item{\code{sample_row_count}}{int; in \strong{rows}; never \code{NA}. Rows carrying this sample.}
\item{\code{column_name}}{string; never \code{NA}. The header's own spelling; characteristics[age] and characteristics[Age] are two columns.}
\item{\code{column_kind}}{string; never \code{NA}. source_name | characteristic | factor_value.}
\item{\code{position}}{int; \code{NA} when status is conflicting: the column was withheld, so it has no positions. 0-based occurrence of a repeated column.}
\item{\code{status}}{string; never \code{NA}. agreed | conflicting (the sample's rows disagree; mzLib withheld the column).}
\item{\code{value}}{string; \code{NA} when status is conflicting (withheld, not absent). The cell verbatim, reserved words included.}
\item{\code{age_years}}{float; in \strong{years}; \code{NA} when not a characteristics[age] row, or the cell was refused (age_refusal says why). The age, a range's midpoint, or a bound.}
\item{\code{age_min_years}}{float; in \strong{years}; \code{NA} when as age_years. Youngest the cell allows; 0 for UpperBound.}
\item{\code{age_max_years}}{float; in \strong{years}; \code{NA} when not an age row; refused; OR precision is LowerBound, meaning UNBOUNDED (mzLib's +infinity, which JSON cannot carry). Oldest the cell allows.}
\item{\code{age_precision}}{string; \code{NA} when not an age row, or refused. Exact | Range | LowerBound | UpperBound (SdrfAgePrecision).}
\item{\code{age_follows_specification}}{bool; \code{NA} when not an age row, or refused. true for nYnMnD / nW grammar, false for unambiguous words.}
\item{\code{age_refusal}}{string; \code{NA} when not an age row, or the cell was read. empty | reserved_word | no_unit | unreadable. Classified by the bridge; mzLib's TryParse answers only true/false.}
}
